  <title>Command palette</title>

<p>The command palette lists the actions of <app>Pano Terminal</app> with
  their shortcuts, your profiles and the open tabs, and finds them by their
  name.</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press <keyseq><key>Shift</key><key>Ctrl</key><key>P</key></keyseq>.</p></item>
<item><p>Type a few letters of the words you are looking for. For example, <input>spl rig</input> finds <gui>Split Right</gui>.</p></item>
<item><p>Press <key>Enter</key> to run the selected entry, or <key>Esc</key> to close the palette.</p></item>
</steps>

  <p>For each profile, the palette offers to open a new tab or window with it,
  or to use it in the current terminal. For each tab, it offers to go
  there.</p>

